cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OmniOmics: an integrated desktop environment for reproducible multi-omics analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Angelo Felipe"
    family-names: "Barbosa de Oliveira"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0831-447X"
    affiliation: "Programa de Pós-Graduação em Genética e Biologia Molecular, Universidade Federal do Pará (UFPA), Belém, PA, Brazil"
version: "0.0.11-alpha"
date-released: "2026-09-14"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oliv-angelus/OmniOmics"
abstract: >-
  OmniOmics is a desktop application that packages five Snakemake workflows for
  metagenomics, metatranscriptomics, isolate genomics, differential expression
  and amplicon sequencing behind a graphical interface, together with an
  integrated plotting environment that turns each workflow's output into
  publication-ready figures. It is aimed at researchers who need reproducible
  multi-omics analysis without assembling and maintaining the toolchain by hand.
  This is an alpha release, validated against synthetic control datasets; a
  stable release and a large-dataset benchmark are planned for December 2026 and
  will be reported in the accompanying manuscript, currently in preparation.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - metagenomics
  - metatranscriptomics
  - amplicon sequencing
  - Snakemake
  - reproducibility
